    - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:baffet-primitive-stretched-debye-2d-energy
  status: verified
  fact_type: energy_identity
  review_level: verified
  claim_policy: stable_claim
  claim_summary: "Variable-coefficient Baffet-Debye energy has an exact R_sigma remainder and only conditional small-gradient monotonicity."
  verification: verify-20260709T035701313438Z-fact-verify-the-variable-coefficient-baf
  ---
  
  ## statement
  
  For the Baffet-Debye primitive system with a=sigma_x(x)+sigma_y(y), b=sigma_x sigma_y, sigma_x,sigma_y nonnegative and sufficiently smooth on Omega_+={a>0}, the Baffet energy in tex/variable_coefficient_baffet_energy_analysis.tex satisfies dE_B/dt = -D0 + R_sigma + B with R_sigma = - integral_{Omega_+} u grad(a) dot lambda and boundary flux B = integral_{partial Omega_+} (u_t+a u) lambda dot n. The displayed D0 is nonnegative under sigma_x,sigma_y>=0 and positive material parameters. Monotonicity is not implied by sigma_i' >= 0 because lambda_i has no fixed sign. If B<=0 and D0 controls m_u||u||^2 + m_lambda||lambda||^2 with m_u,m_lambda>0 and ||grad a||_infty^2 < 4 m_u m_lambda, then dE_B/dt + theta D0 <= 0 for some theta>0; without such absorption one obtains at most a Gronwall-type bound from this energy.
  
  ## notes
  
  Generated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.
  ---
  fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:port-layer-energy-not-pml
  problem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_project: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration
  source_task: task-v5-variable-coefficient-baffet
  predecessors: []
  status: verified
  fact_type: energy_obstruction
  review_level: verified
  claim_policy: stable_claim
  claim_summary: "The port layer has a monotone energy but fails the strict PML admittance test for oblique modes."
  verification: verify-20260709T040228930557Z-fact-verify-the-port-layer-energy-identi
  ---
  
  ## statement
  
  For the port model epsilon E_t + P_t + epsilon sigma_E E = partial_x W_y - partial_y W_x, mu W_{x,t}+mu sigma_y W_x=-partial_y E, mu W_{y,t}+mu sigma_x W_y=partial_x E, tau P_t+P=kappa E, the positive energy 1/2 integral (epsilon E^2+mu W_x^2+mu W_y^2+kappa^{-1}P^2) satisfies dE_port/dt plus integral(epsilon sigma_E E^2+mu sigma_y W_x^2+mu sigma_x W_y^2+tau kappa^{-1}P_t^2) equals the boundary flux integral E(W_y n_x-W_x n_y). However, in an x-PML with sigma_x=sigma>0 and sigma_y=0, the Laplace-Fourier admittance obeys Y_port^2-Y_0^2=(epsilon sigma_E-sigma epsilon_D(s))/(mu(s+sigma))-sigma k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+sigma)). Therefore no scalar local sigma_E makes Y_port=Y_0 for all oblique modes k_y, so the port model is a stable absorbing layer, not a strict perfectly matched layer, although it reduces to Maxwell-Debye when all damping vanishes.
  
  ## notes
  
  Generated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.
